	.type	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4826,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4826,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4826:
	.ascii	"A shape targeted via sh:targetWhere selects the nodes that conform to another shape, not a class extension; it has no closed-world JSON Schema $def and its constraints are not enforced by the emitted schema."
	.size	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4826, 207

	.type	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4827,@object
	.section	.rodata.cst16,"aM",@progbits,16
.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4827:
	.ascii	"sh:uniqueMembers"
	.size	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4827, 16

	.type	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4828,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4828,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4828:
	.ascii	"A SHACL 1.2 sh:uniqueMembers constraint (true: no repeated member; false: only a list) judges a list value node or focus node (as uniqueItems); the instance projection carries a list JSON-LD 1.1 converts (Processing Algorithms and API 8.4.2) as its @list array, which the schema judges exactly; a list it keeps as linked @graph nodes (a cell with another property, referenced twice, or an IRI) is a node reference whose members hang off other @graph nodes, and a JSON Schema keyword judges only the instance location it applies to and those beneath it ($ref resolves schemas, never instance values), so for such a value the constraint is not checked. On a node shape the focus node's own member (its rdf:first) is not compared with the members of its rdf:rest, two instance locations no JSON Schema keyword relates."
	.size	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4828, 815

	.type	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4829,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4829,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4829:
	.ascii	"sh:uniqueValuesFor"
	.size	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4829, 18

	.type	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4830,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4830,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4830:
	.ascii	"A SHACL 1.2 sh:uniqueValuesFor constraint forbids two target nodes of a shape from having exactly the same values for the listed properties; a JSON Schema judges one instance alone (uniqueItems is uniqueness within one array, not across instances), so the constraint is dropped."
	.size	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4830, 278

	.type	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4831,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4831,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4831:
	.ascii	"sh:values"
	.size	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4831, 9

	.type	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4832,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4832,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4832:
	.ascii	"A SHACL 1.2 property shape with sh:values takes the output nodes of a node expression evaluated at validation as value nodes, which a JSON document does not carry; projecting its constraints onto the document's own values would require what a computed value supplies, so the property shape is dropped."
	.size	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4832, 301

	.type	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4833,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4833,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4833:
	.ascii	"sh:defaultValue"
	.size	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4833, 15

	.type	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4834,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4834,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4834:
	.ascii	"A SHACL 1.2 property shape with sh:defaultValue takes the output nodes of a node expression as its value nodes when the property has no other value; a JSON document does not carry them, and projecting the shape's constraints onto the document's own values would require what the default supplies, so the property shape is dropped."
	.size	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4834, 330

	.type	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4835,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4835,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4835:
	.ascii	"sh:and"
	.size	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4835, 6

	.type	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4836,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4836,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4836:
	.ascii	"A sh:and constraint on a property shape judges each value node against shapes; a value is projected as a node reference (its own properties live on its separate @graph node) or a literal, so the value schema has nothing to judge and the constraint is dropped."
	.size	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4836, 259

	.type	.Lanon.0baec5b44c5538d1487548c085149cb7.4837,@object
